{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01HiW4J2S8Y6R8671fiq8dWB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. **Q20: F1 score, ROC curve** is written and committed.\n\n**What the note covers:**\n- **F1** = harmonic mean of precision & recall; **F-beta** when false negatives vs false positives have asymmetric costs (β=2 for medical, β=0.5 for spam)\n- **AUC-ROC** = threshold-free rank quality (use to *compare* models); plots TPR vs FPR across all thresholds\n- **PR-AUC** (average precision) = preferred for imbalanced datasets where positives are rare (fraud 0.1%) — ROC is optimistic because FPR is diluted by the huge TN pool\n- **Threshold tuning**: separate from model selection — tune on the PR curve against `cost = FP_rate × FP_cost + FN_rate × FN_cost`\n- **Multi-class**: macro F1 penalises minority class failures equally; weighted F1 tracks production volume\n- Pitfalls: using accuracy on imbalanced data, defaulting to AUC-ROC for rare-positive tasks, conflating model comparison (AUC) with threshold selection\n\nNext up: **Q21: Linear vs logistic regression**."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":339,"cache_read_input_tokens":70423,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":339,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b29b6295-309c-4d63-b123-8b007e1a8f23","uuid":"2193156b-f9f7-4ea6-98f3-fc09c8d43e40"}
